{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas","id":1316551,"title":"Is there a way to stop Voormas?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-06-04T20:52:14-07:00","id":1316551,"title":"Is there a way to stop Voormas?","content":"If so, how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T01:28:39-07:00","id":1316576,"title":"","content":"I think the end time book for mage lists a way to do it using a ritual but I forget how, really I think getting him to commit suicide would kill im off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T01:56:14-07:00","id":1316580,"title":"","content":"It somewhat depends on what you mean by stop him. Stopping him/killing him isn't really that hard. Stopping his legacy is a much, much harder thing, since he encoded his beliefs into his own death, twisting however kills him to follow in his footsteps (and whoever kills them to as well, etc.). This basically means you have to have a series of individuals all willing to die in a row, each progressively magically weaker, until you've got someone that Voormas's legacy can't manifest strongly in, and then figure out a way to get rid of it (it's not clear if suicide would work, but probably).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T02:00:30-07:00","id":1316582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1316580#post1316580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It somewhat depends on what you mean by stop him. Stopping him/killing him isn't really that hard. Stopping his legacy is a much, much harder thing, since he encoded his beliefs into his own death, twisting however kills him to follow in his footsteps (and whoever kills them to as well, etc.). This basically means you have to have a series of individuals all willing to die in a row, each progressively magically weaker, until you've got someone that Voormas's legacy can't manifest strongly in, and then figure out a way to get rid of it (it's not clear if suicide would work, but probably).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the first thought that came to mind when I read the commentary about &quot;making him commit suicide&quot;. First his Jhor is based on fear of death, so I think it would make it hard for him to want to commit suicide and second he has this nasty ritual/effect of passing his goals to whoever kills him. And third, but not least, he is one of the most powerful creatures in the World of Darkness, so it's basically night impossible to find someone able to kill him in the first place...and then you have the &quot;curse&quot; passing on etc. Really tricky situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T02:15:58-07:00","id":1316584,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you can manage to murder this guy (Who, depending on the book, has like entropy 9) getting him to kill himself can't be too far from the realms of possibility.<br /> <br /> TBH if you know about the curse you might be able to use spirit/time/entropy/some other crazy magickal effect to counter it completely. Maybe use a lot of opposite resonance, a resonance of life or something, and a lot of other stuff.<br /> <br /> Or give it to some sleeper who's useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T02:46:15-07:00","id":1316589,"title":"","content":"Voormas isn't that hard to kill. Sure he has Entropy 7 in his most powerful write-up, but actually using high level Spheres in combat isn't exactly easy. Plus there's a magically blade out there that was made just for killing him. A cabal of PCs at the end of a decently long campaign really aren't going to go in the under-dogs when facing him in direct conflict (even if losing a few is probable). You just have to hope that whoever kills him rolls really well on that WP check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T02:57:37-07:00","id":1316591,"title":"","content":"But then again some possibly interesting things come to mind. What if the one who kills him isn't a mage, but a cainite or a werewolf? Or what about imprisioning his soul in an object like an &quot;Egg of Korshei&quot; of sorts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-05-2019, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T04:18:43-07:00","id":1316595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1316591#post1316591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the one who kills him isn't a mage, but a cainite or a werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>This post concerns what you say, maybe it can help you:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/962769-a-question-regarding-a-certain-gift/page2\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ain-gift/page2</a><br /> <br /> They compare him with Zhyzak, maybe the most powerful canon werewolf. I haven't re-read this, but I remember the answer is Voormas will win anyway. <br /> <br /> And one guy says he is much more powerful than average Meths vampire.<br /> <br /> So maybe you need several Rank 6 Shapeshifters or Incarna, really powerful Meths or even Antes to kill him. A big crossover.<br /> <br /> \u203bUh but in my opinion I will oppose this kind of big crossover, All splats have godlike guys and they should be ST Only for Plot Device... I won't assume who will win when mage the Unnamed versus Antes...never mind. <br /> <br /> But in theory all guys having stats are killable.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And it may be very difficult to compare different splats' powers because of their traits. Another reason I avoid crossover...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 06-05-2019, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T08:32:43-07:00","id":1316641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1316591#post1316591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then again some possibly interesting things come to mind. What if the one who kills him isn't a mage, but a cainite or a werewolf? Or what about imprisioning his soul in an object like an &quot;Egg of Korshei&quot; of sorts?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a non-mage kills him? They'd still end up cursed by his legacy and - recognizing that they can't perform his plans in that state - get themselves killed by attacking a powerful mage to pass it on to them.<br /> <br /> Trying to imprison his soul in Mage would generally result in his body dying, thus count as killing him for however casts the spell; and worse that person could then have Voormas's soul around too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1316595#post1316595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This post concerns what you say, maybe it can help you:</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Internet debates about crossover fights are rarely that informative. Two NPCs that are meant to be big fights towards the end of a major metaplot event are designed to be interesting for that fight, not for squaring off against each other.<br /> <br /> They're also designed for their games, not for crossover stuff. What has people claiming Voormas is so hard to beat in crossover are things like his stats letting him turn his blades to silver to do lots of unsoakable damage to werewolves, because in Mage that's not really a big deal, and it's not going to help you kill other mages, but in Werewolf it's a huge deal.<br /> <br /> And that's the thing. Voormas is designed to be taken down by mages... and has a bunch of weaknesses you don't have to be that powerful of a mage to exploit, or think of exploiting. Most characters from other splats aren't necessarily going to have the powers to do it, or know to even think of it. Because beating Voormas is about fighting like a mage: fighting smart, not hard. Going after Voormas with some super powered vampires with 7+ in the physical Disciplines is dumb, because that's a fight Voormas is designed to win. Throw a measly starting level Ravnos that focuses on Chimerstry in their with the knowledge of Voormas's fear of death? And Voormas is going to be wasting lots of time/power cancelling those illusions, and then being insanely vulnerable to physical attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They compare him with Zhyzak, maybe the most powerful canon werewolf. </div> </div> </div>The most <b>physically</b> powerful individual werewolf. Power isn't just based in how big your combat ratings are. She's designed for winning a one-on-one duel with another Garou (it is literally her destiny and she knows it and trains for it), not for being the best all around fighter for her combat level in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in theory all guys having stats are killable. </div> </div> </div>And more importantly, killing Voormas is supposed to be a viable course of events for the Ascension finale. This is not a case of &quot;well it has stats so it's theoretically possible.&quot; You're supposed to be able to do it, even if it's a high difficulty/cost fight meant for high XP characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T10:34:27-07:00","id":1316660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1316641#post1316641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a non-mage kills him? They'd still end up cursed by his legacy and - recognizing that they can't perform his plans in that state - get themselves killed by attacking a powerful mage to pass it on to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be interesting to see how other supernaturals would try to perform his plans. Suicide by Mage sounds plausible, and it would be the optimal way to go if there are other potent mages arround and the apocalipse it's near. In Ascencion that's almost a given.<br /> <br /> Still, I wonder if other consequences are impossible. Inheriting Voormass madness doesn't necesarily means that you will be able to destroy Death yesterday, it merely pushes you towards that goal. It would be feasible to control and groom a mage until it grows powerful enough to cast the spell. And it's not like other splats haven't their own apocaliptic mcguffin powers.<br /> <br /> It could be a way to create an interesting antagonist for a crossover chronicle. The players follow clues to the Archmage, discover his cause, and then find Voormass is dead...but then discover that someone <i>else </i>has inherited his cause and resources, yet it's not a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-05-2019, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T13:47:34-07:00","id":1316695,"title":"","content":"On the Cainite end, I can see Voormas' death curse sending his killer to learn everything they can about the metaphysics of death, which in all likelihood sends them to the Giovanni and their Endless Night master plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T15:37:18-07:00","id":1316717,"title":"","content":"The wording of the curse is that it transfers to the person with the strongest sympathetic tie, which is <i>probably</i> the killer. But another candidate could be Theora, she is Voormas' last remaining apprentice as well as being the one he seems to have had the most influence over. Plus, she's probably not that powerful a mage when the players need to restrain her.<br /> <br /> 'Course, that's a pretty dark way to end things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T20:44:04-07:00","id":1316758,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that (almost) anything is possible, but direct combat probably isn't the best approach.<br /> <br /> In Don't Kill it - there is a demon that possesses the person that kills it.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Spoiler - the creature is banished to hell because the last person to kill the host has pulled pins to a grenade; killing themselves</div></div> </div> </div><br /> So that's a possibility to get around the curse. But I encourage the ability to think around a problem to work in general.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, a group of comparable, or slightly weaker mages that can counter everything that Voormas tries to spit out would make things really hard for him. It's even be possible to counter the curse, or unweave it, from what I understand, but that'd probably take another massive ritual to get the successes to break it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T02:41:11-07:00","id":1316785,"title":"","content":"Something I only just noticed; the curse specifically mentions that it passes to the <b>Awakened</b> with the closest sympathetic tie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T06:10:57-07:00","id":1316805,"title":"","content":"Just surround him and his killer with ordinary accountants and let the Paradox finish him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T08:31:41-07:00","id":1316835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1316805#post1316805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just surround him and his killer with ordinary accountants and let the Paradox finish him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Voormas is an immortal sorcerer who lives in a walking castle. He ain't going anywhere near the <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">consensus</span></span></span>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T16:46:59-07:00","id":1317075,"title":"","content":"In the Deep Lore / Backstory of my game, a Mage came up with a plan to defeat Voormas by tricking him into consuming a soul that would damage him. The plan was flawed since Voormas is an archmage with incredible Awareness/Arete/senses, but thanks to the effects of Quiet Voormas fell for the trap (or did he? See below), being unable to resist such a powerful soul.<br /> <br /> Drinking the souls prepared by Erebus (a character I've invented; he wasn't a powerful Mage at the time by setting standards, he needed the help of more powerful mages to actually execute this plan) he became irreparably damaged, leaving him just vulnerable enough that he could be destroyed.<br /> <br /> Erebus was then lauded as a hero, and he used this fame and adoration to form a new movement within the Order of Hermes which sought to purge the Traditions of &quot;backwards, individualist&quot; thinking. The Erebus movement was essentially aiming to make the Traditions into a mystical equivalent of the Technocracy; a unified vision where personal belief was overridden by mutualism. Not that any of them would describe it like that; the pitch would be &quot;We need to be united to defeat the Technocracy, we need to offer an alternative, and that means us all agreeing on some central ideas and sticking to them. Once we've won we can begin to return to a softer and more diverse approach to magick within the Traditions&quot;. Because Erebus became something of a &quot;big bad&quot;, many Mages in-setting have speculated that he was somehow corrupted by Voormas.<br /> <br /> Word of God from me would be no, he wasn't corrupted. He wasn't a Marauder or Nephandus or anything like that, and he wasn't the &quot;heir to Voormas' curse&quot;. But it's very important that people make *excuses* along those lines. No, there is NOTHING wrong with the culture of the Order of Hermes. Erebus was just a bad person who did bad things because he was bad. Those who followed him were either irredeemably evil (read: they died in the conflict) or were misguided (read: they surrendered at the end of the conflict).<br /> <br /> Did Voormas actually fall for the trap? It could be argued that he allowed himself to be destroyed, or to seem to be destroyed, as part of some higher scheme or plan. Although the most likely explanation is simply that like many mages he lost control of his actions to a Quiet and faced deadly repercussions. The *power* to sense a trap is nothing if you are not in the right state to use it.<br /> <br /> Voormas is going to be &quot;reincarnated&quot; within the story. A young boy who collects moths and butterflies, pinning them down so that they can be beautiful forever (a metaphor for Voormas' plans for reality; a static world where he would never allow death to occur). When the Euthanatos get wind that his Avatar has returned they will arrive and create drama, demanding that Voormas be executed for his High Crimes etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-07T17:26:19-07:00","id":1317080,"title":"","content":"Has no one brought up &quot;Embrace him&quot; yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T00:31:44-07:00","id":1317129,"title":"","content":"A. Look into the book Ascension, as it discusses how to defeat the character.<br /> B. Use magic to prevent him watching the final season of <i>Game of Thrones</i> - he only started trying to destroy the world as he watched the final season and handled his disappointment badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T03:45:15-07:00","id":1317148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1317080#post1317080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has no one brought up &quot;Embrace him&quot; yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably that would still transfer the curse. It seems tied to the Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T12:06:47-07:00","id":1317220,"title":"","content":"Yes, that would just change a little the means by which he would try to accomplish his goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T00:01:22-07:00","id":1320906,"title":"","content":"For a sufficiently over the top ending, you bring him before Kali's Avatar and she sets him straight.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-26T06:29:37-07:00","id":1320945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1320906#post1320906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a sufficiently over the top ending, you bring him before Kali's Avatar and she sets him straight.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that he defeated an aspect of Kali in her own Realm to <i>become </i>her in order to get past the <i>real</i> Shiva...I think that may not be sufficently over the top. Sure, it's possible in the sense that you can put that Avatar any Traits you want, but it would be kinda underwhelming of an end if he can't do <i>anything </i>against that and <i>just dies</i>, in my opinion, considering all that he went trough.<br /> <br /> Now, tricking (or forcing) Vormass into meeting the <i>actual </i>Incarna/Aeon of Kali in a Realm where she can manifest her <i>full power </i>after having convinced her of destroying him. That would be <i>quite </i>over the top.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not sure what Kali would think about being asked to destroy an aspect of herself, even if it's a debased and corrupt aspect. Maybe it's the chance she was waiting all this time to get rid of that embarasment...but maybe she isn't going to be that hostile, much like Shiva wasn't. Perhaps she would need to be convinced that Voormas is just <i>wearing</i> that aspect to fool the gods before becoming suitably angry. In any case, it would make an interesting roleplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T22:07:46-07:00","id":1330880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1317080#post1317080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has no one brought up &quot;Embrace him&quot; yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;drain the victim of blood&quot; part is tricky when the subject can just make more blood, and also specify it turns corrosive when it leaves his body, and anyway he was warned this might happen last week in a dream.<br /> <br /> I think Voormas would enjoy taking some vampire blood into his system, encysting it, and using it as an intimate sympathetic connection to enslave the vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T22:08:58-07:00","id":1330881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas#post1316551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, how?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Easy. Destroy the universe, like last time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T12:25:32-07:00","id":1331829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1316805#post1316805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just surround him and his killer with ordinary accountants and let the Paradox finish him.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1316551-is-there-a-way-to-stop-voormas?p=1316835#post1316835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voormas is an immortal sorcerer who lives in a walking castle. He ain't going anywhere near the <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">consensus</span></span></span>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just put a post on Facebook like, &quot;Hey everyone, remember our successful raid into Area 51? Well there's this creepy castle that's said to be haunted. So we're going to go flush out all of the ghosts on X date! Everyone get together and we're going to Naruto-run our way through this castle and see if we can spot any spooky ghosts!&quot;<br /> <br /> Can you imagine Voormas' letting out a Darth Vader style &quot;NOOOOOOOO!&quot; in absolute horror as thousands of Sleepers dressed in Naruto cosplay descend on his castle and start running around wrecking all of his carefully laid plans? Yeah, yeah, I know it wouldn't happen because of so many reasons but I got a kick out of imagining it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T14:41:11-07:00","id":1332025,"title":"","content":"Imagine the Euthanatos, Akashics, and Ecstatics working together to pull thousands (or maybe even hundreds of thousands) of Sleepers into a shared dream in which they experience visions of Voormas' plot playing out, then are all waked up simultaneously with the idea &quot;Whew! It was just a dream. Nothing that fantastical could ever have been real!&quot; inceptioned into their minds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-22T07:07:10-07:00","id":1332121,"title":"","content":"Well, the main problem for any of these ideas it's that he's in the Umbra...<br /> <br /> ....but then, if you were able to open a series of really big portals trough the Umbra connecting Vormass Realm and the desert, while creating an illusion in all the area covered by the portals except the last one (the one opening to Voormass castle) making people believe they're walking trough the desert. And *then* convinced a horde of Area 51 raid turists that this is <i>totally </i>the way to Area 51...<br /> <br /> Now *that* ... wouldn't work either for a lot of reasons ... but it would get closer. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T14:34:13-07:00","id":1332473,"title":"","content":"Has anyone considered debating him yet? I'm tired of these no-good thuggish mages trying to solve problems with violence; I think it's only right that we challenge Voormas in the marketplace of ideas and allow free speech and rationality to fix-<br /> <br /> *before he can finish speaking, he is torn apart at the most basic level, pulled into a screeching entropic void of endless undeath, and his dying words of &quot;so much for the tolerant left&quot; are barely audible*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-24T23:15:03-07:00","id":1332502,"title":"","content":"There is mention if you can scare him into fearing his own death (I think implied with magick) he goes crazy for a bit and leaves you alone.<br /> <br /> So debate his ass into thinking he'll die in the next few minutes and we have enough time to get the fuck out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T04:55:19-07:00","id":1332634,"title":"","content":"It's something to note that Vormass likes to talk. He really likes to. In the end of the world, if characters talk to him, he will try to convince them of his masterplan (which implies explaining it, of course. That's the 90's cartoon villan we know and love <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> He's also pretty good at it (and pretty good at twisting minds with magick - heck, according to some he did that to a whole vampire clan) ... so, it's by no means insta-win, but for a really good social wizard it may be the way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}